# Before working on MailCheap

Read `AGENTS.md` at the repository root: how the app is organized, MailCheap Cloud and self-hosting, the open source boundary, naming, code style and tests.

In MailCheap Cloud's own repository, `AGENTS.cloud.md` is next to it: read it too, for what stays private, the sync to the open source, deploys and worktrees.

Any change the people using MailCheap can see, or to how something works, updates the help center (`app/(site)/help`) in the same commit. Articles link to the dashboard pages they mention, with `LinkApp`.

Every public content page ends on a call to action: the help center and the docs, and in MailCheap Cloud's repository the guides, comparisons, changelog and landing sections (AGENTS.md, and "Calls to action" in AGENTS.cloud.md).

Every feature or significant change gets a security review before it ships: run the security-review subagent on its diff (split a large one), fix what it rates medium or higher first, and go through the checklist in AGENTS.md's "Security review".
